  "limitations": [
    "Single supervisor is the exclusive namespace manager for a generated local directory with mode 0700. Conditional removal by inode in an arbitrarily mutable directory is unsupported.",
    "Pending bootstrap may create its own sidecars before detecting a mismatched catalog writer inside the live SQLite transaction. Export side effects require activation.",
    "A private fixture uses an inherited socket/nonce and environment to configure the worker; release must bind capability inside the trusted executor, pin its SQLite backend and define supervisor restart/drain policy.",
    "Process-death fixture explicitly checkpointed the catalog and retained a zero-byte WAL before exiting. Recovery of committed but uncheckpointed frames without the original live witness is not established.",
    "Limited to actual Linux AArch64 FILESTAT/Procfs and kernel primitives in this runtime. Apple SQLite, security-scoped bookmarks, external volumes, hot rollback, power loss and end-to-end throughput were not measured."
